From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:43:07 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2767/2769] rtc: surface: Describe the driver

The driver came with a placeholder help text and a header comment
copied from the Surface AC driver. Say what it is for: SAM keeps the
time on these Surfaces, and the driver reads and sets SAM's Unix
timestamp. SAM also keeps the time zone Windows set, which the firmware
adds when it reports local time; the driver leaves it alone.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/rtc/Kconfig       | 9 ++++++++-
 drivers/rtc/rtc-surface.c | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/rtc/Kconfig b/drivers/rtc/Kconfig
index abe2c85..bb2ee83 100644
--- a/drivers/rtc/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/rtc/Kconfig
@@ -1430,7 +1430,14 @@ config RTC_DRV_SURFACE
 	depends on SURFACE_AGGREGATOR
 	depends on SURFACE_AGGREGATOR_BUS
 	help
-	  TODO
+	  Real-time clock of Microsoft Surface devices that keep the time in
+	  the Surface System Aggregator Module (SAM), the Surface's embedded
+	  controller, such as the Surface Laptop 8. The driver reads and sets
+	  SAM's Unix timestamp; the time zone SAM keeps for Windows is left
+	  alone.
+
+	  This driver can also be built as a module. If so, the module will
+	  be called rtc-surface.
 
 comment "on-CPU RTC drivers"
 
diff --git a/drivers/rtc/rtc-surface.c b/drivers/rtc/rtc-surface.c
index f6c17c4..4cb3773 100644
--- a/drivers/rtc/rtc-surface.c
+++ b/drivers/rtc/rtc-surface.c
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0+
 /*
- * AC driver for 7th-generation Microsoft Surface devices via Surface System
- * Aggregator Module (SSAM).
+ * RTC driver for Microsoft Surface devices whose real-time clock is kept by
+ * the Surface System Aggregator Module (SSAM).
